From 98e950e42a26c50f84d2112a0c0050a0e797797e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pseudo <cdodge@pseudoseed.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:51:07 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 21/33] [Spec 250][Phase: phase_8] fix: the row marker is the
 gate name and a gavel, not 'Gate: <name>'
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two placements were tried and both lost something to the same ~230px. On the
line above the title, 'Gate: verify-approval' plus the 'Architect' caption plus
the timestamp overflow, and the caption truncated to 'A…'. Moved to the title
line, the marker fit and the TITLE truncated instead — the row's primary
identifier, on every gated row.

The label is the gate name alone now, and the word is carried by the panel's own
gavel. Six characters bought back the room: the caption, the gate and the title
all survive, and the row and the panel say 'gate' the same way.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
